<section id="changes"><span class="compat-anchor" id="release-summary-title" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2>Nine releases since the previous site snapshot</h2>
<div class="guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Changes since version 0.26">
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Release</th><th scope="col">What changed</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">0.34 · gateway name</th><td data-label="What changed"><code>dekopond</code> becomes <code>dekopon-gatewayd</code>, including its config API and environment variables. Chart {{ release.chart.publishedVersion }} and console 0.8.0 target this release.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">0.33 · child scripts</th><td data-label="What changed">A provider can ask the gateway to run a child script through <code>dekopon:spawn</code>. The child shares the caller's execution tree, budget and trace; it does not gain a new identity or wider grants.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">0.32 · offline compilation</th><td data-label="What changed">Managed provider sets require precompiled artifacts before broker startup. Providers can read monotonic time and bounded OS entropy during invocation.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">0.31 · provider streams</th><td data-label="What changed"><code>provider@0.4.0</code> reads stdin and writes stdout through bounded streams, returning an exit status. Per-agent token budgets and a metered guest model proxy also ship.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">0.30 · background jobs</th><td data-label="What changed">Routes that set <code>limits.jobTimeoutMs</code> can run detached jobs with <code>&amp;</code>. Use <code>jobs</code>, <code>wait</code> and <code>kill</code>; a restart loses those jobs.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">0.29 · byte pipelines</th><td data-label="What changed">Pipes preserve bytes and newlines. Non-final compound and function stages isolate their variables; <code>jq</code> consumes JSON text, while ordinary filters produce text.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">0.28 / 0.28.1 · bounded workers</th><td data-label="What changed"><code>jq</code> runs in a killable, memory-limited worker process. Guest memory is charged as it grows; the patch release fixes compiled-cache reuse after an engine change.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">0.27 · skills and secrets</th><td data-label="What changed">An example teaches agents to save learned skills in agent-scoped Turso storage. Broker-private Kubernetes TokenRequest credentials arrive here; OAuth2 refresh sources follow in 0.28.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
