<section id="migration"><span class="compat-anchor" id="release-details-title" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="compat-anchor" id="release-path-title" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2>Upgrade the provider set and both daemons together</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Replace old components.</strong> Brokers reject <code>provider@0.3.0</code>. Install compatible components explicitly: core archives and images no longer bundle out-of-tree providers. Recheck the HTTP contract; the current broker links <code>client@1.1.0</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Prepare startup.</strong> Run <code>dekopon-brokerd provider precompile</code> for the broker's engine before starting a managed set. Chart 0.21 and newer supply the precompile init container. Roll the gateway with the broker for the changed protocol.</li>
<li><strong>Migrate gateway configuration.</strong> Rename the binary and its config API to <code>dekopon.dev/gatewayd/v1alpha1</code>. Update deployment paths and environment variables; preserve journal state at its new path. Review shell scripts that assumed JSON-value pipes.</li>
</ol>
<p>The <a href="{{ source }}/docs/upgrading.md">pinned upgrade guide ↗</a> gives exact renamed fields and the intervening breaking changes. <a href="/deploy/kubernetes/">The Kubernetes recipe</a> pins the verified current image independently of the chart's historical tag label.</p>
</section>
<section id="limits"><span class="compat-anchor" id="release-scope-title" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2>Optional features need explicit configuration</h2>
<p>Background jobs are off until a route grants a timeout. Learned skills need the catalog skill and storage grant. Token budgets need configured limits; boot restore needs a supported telemetry backend. None of these enable themselves by upgrading.</p>
<p>Provider-vm 0.3.0 and vm-runner 0.3.0 add a separate VM execution path for browser and document tooling. The <code>ssh</code> command word calls the runner's API; it is not an SSH connection or a host-shell escape. Deploy and constrain that service separately.</p>
<p>Dekopon is still pre-production. Cedar checks declared access, not intent. A permitted endpoint can reflect a credential it receives, and telemetry retention remains your responsibility.</p>
</section>
